{
  "title": "Cleansing the Teeth",
  "data": "Before the ritual ablution (wudu’), brush the teeth with the miswak (a stick used for cleansing the teeth).\nIf a miswak is not available, it is sufficient to use one’s finger.",
  "merits": "Brushing the teeth with the miswak cleanses the mouth, removes phlegm, strengthens the memory, increases the good deeds, and pleases the Exalted Lord. A two-unit prayer that is preceded by cleansing the teeth is more favorable than a seventy-unit prayer without it."
}
